Core Philosophy
Since combat is automated with limited player interaction, the initial character build and long-term stat progression become the primary strategic layer. Gear adds tactical variety but doesn't override core identity.

1. Base Stats (6-14 at Level 1, slow growth)
Each base stat starts with a racial baseline + age modifier + backstory modifier + size modifier, then gains +1 per 4 levels (approx +5 by level 20).

Stat	Primary Function	Secondary Function
Strength (STR)	Physical Attack, Carry Capacity	HP (minor), Armor (heavy)
Agility (AGI)	Dodge, Physical Crit Chance	Speed, Physical Attack (finesse)
Constitution (CON)	HP, Physical Resist	Mana (minor), Armor
Perception (PER)	Crit Chance (all), Initiative	Magical Attack (accuracy), Dodge (anti-ambush)
Intelligence (INT)	Mana, Magical Attack	Magical Resist, Crit Damage
Charisma (CHA)	Support skills, Buff Duration	Magical Resist (willpower), Initiative (leadership)
Level scaling formula for base stats:

text
Base Stat = Racial_Base + Age_Mod + Backstory_Mod + Size_Mod + floor(Level / 4)
*Range at level 1: 6-14 | Range at level 20: 11-19 (+ racial/age/size/backstory modifiers)*

