7. Automated Combat Balance
Since combat is automated, these systems ensure balance:

Turn Order
text
Action_Speed = Speed + (PER × 0.5) + (Level × 0.3)
Higher action speed = acts first and more frequently (round-robin with weighting)

Target Selection AI (configurable per character)
Tank: Prioritize enemies attacking allies, use taunt

Damage: Attack lowest HP% or highest threat

Support: Heal lowest HP%, buff strongest ally

Control: Debuff highest damage enemy

Damage Reduction Order
Dodge check → negate all damage if successful

Block check (shield) → reduce by 50% if successful

Armor reduction → Damage × (100 / (100 + Armor))

Resistance reduction (magical only) → Damage × (1 - Resist%)

Flat reduction (from gear/abilities)

Example Combat Log (Level 5 Dwarf Fighter vs Level 5 Elf Mage)
text
Turn 1: Dwarf (Speed 18) attacks Elf (Speed 22)
  - Elf dodges? 15% dodge → roll 42 → hit
  - Damage: Physical Attack 45 + Axe 14 = 59
  - Armor reduces: 59 × (100/135) = 44 damage
  - Elf HP: 85 → 41

Turn 2: Elf casts Firebolt
  - Magical Attack 52 + Staff 8 = 60
  - Dwarf Magic Resist 25% → 45 damage
  - Dwarf HP: 110 → 65

